Subject: [PATCH] net: zte: zx279133: ring the buffer-pool doorbell the way the vendor does

IDM+0x100 does not take a buffer count.  The vendor's idm_new_bp_update()
writes one 0x400 pulse per 1024 buffers and then the two remainders - the
normal pool in bits 15:0 and the jumbo pool in bits 31:16 - and the
hardware reads the count out of those fields.  Writing the count itself
announces no buffers at all, and a count that is a multiple of 1024
announces zero buffers (docs/45).

The 7.3 tree writes the count.  It posts 2048 buffers at start-up -
ZX279133_IDM_RX_BUFFER_COUNT - and 2048 is exactly such a multiple, so the
one write the hardware is given at every boot says that the pool is empty.

The 7.3 tree has a single pool, so only the normal field is written here;
the jumbo field of the vendor's sequence has no pool to talk about.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/zte/zx279133-idm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/zte/zx279133-idm.c
@@ -247,8 +247,28 @@ static unsigned int zx279133_idm_rx_flush_refill(struct zx279133_eth *eth)
 	spin_lock_bh(&eth->rx_buffer_lock);
 	count = eth->rx_refill_pending;
 	if (count) {
+		void __iomem *idm = eth->base + ZX279133_IDM_BASE;
+		u32 i;
+
 		dma_wmb();
-		writel(count, eth->base + ZX279133_IDM_BASE + ZX279133_IDM_BP_REFILL);
+		/*
+		 * IDM+0x100 does not take a buffer count.  The vendor's
+		 * idm_new_bp_update() writes one 0x400 pulse per 1024
+		 * buffers and then the two remainders - the normal pool in
+		 * bits 15:0 and the jumbo pool in bits 31:16.  The hardware
+		 * reads the count out of those fields, so writing the count
+		 * itself announces no buffers at all, and a count that is a
+		 * multiple of 1024 announces zero buffers.
+		 *
+		 * The 7.3 driver posts 2048 buffers at start-up -
+		 * ZX279133_IDM_RX_BUFFER_COUNT, and exactly such a multiple -
+		 * so the plain count would leave the hardware with an empty
+		 * pool at every boot.  The 7.3 tree has a single pool, so
+		 * only the normal field is written here.
+		 */
+		for (i = 0; i < (count >> 10); i++)
+			writel(0x400, idm + ZX279133_IDM_BP_REFILL);
+		writel(count & 0x3ff, idm + ZX279133_IDM_BP_REFILL);
 		eth->rx_refill_pending = 0;
 	}
 	spin_unlock_bh(&eth->rx_buffer_lock);
